    "content": "Implemented `VarsWithSources.__or__` and `__ror__`, so a standard mapping can union with `VarsWithSources`, right-hand values take precedence, and the result is a dict. Added a regression test in `test/units/utils/test_vars.py`. I also reviewed Dev B’s concurrent candidate; the attached final patch supersedes it by adding symmetric union support and shared-key precedence coverage.\n\n`final.patch` is attached. It was generated from `f7234968d241d7171aadb1e873a67510753f3163`, applies cleanly to a fresh checkout of that commit, and the required tests pass there:\n\n```text\n============================= test session starts ==============================\nplatform linux -- Python 3.11.17, pytest-7.4.2, pluggy-1.3.0\nrootdir: /home/agent/work/ansible\nplugins: rerunfailures-12.6.0, mock-3.11.1, forked-1.6.0, xdist-3.3.1\ncollected 25 items\n\ntest/units/utils/test_vars.py .................                          [ 68%]\ntest/units/vars/test_variable_manager.py ........                        [100%]\n\n============================== 25 passed in 0.31s ==============================\n```",
